{
  "id": "ep173",
  "duration": 51.501,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.548,
      "text": "NASA never spent millions developing a space pen.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Art Institute of Chicago (CC0)",
        "title": "Marriage Consultation",
        "credit": "Edward Fisher\nIrish, 1730-1785",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://www.artic.edu/artworks/80167"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.533,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.548,
      "end": 7.918,
      "text": "Early U.S. and Soviet missions relied on standard pencils.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Sharpened pencil next to sheet paper.jpg",
        "credit": "Thomaseagle",
        "license": "CC BY 3.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sharpened_pencil_next_to_sheet_paper.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.533,
          "end": 6.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 6.4,
          "end": 7.933,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 7.918,
      "end": 15.838,
      "text": "However, broken pencil graphite tips and wood shavings posed electrical shorts and eye hazards in zero gravity.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "STS-135 final flyaround of ISS 1.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:STS-135_final_flyaround_of_ISS_1.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 7.933,
          "end": 11.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 11.933,
          "end": 15.833,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 15.838,
      "end": 21.783,
      "text": "Pencils also presented a severe fire hazard in spacecraft oxygen environments.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Command and Service Modules, Apollo -105, ASTP Mockup - DPLA - a0ec1c586f20e26eb3f3b857f4fd819b (page 2).jpg",
        "credit": "North American Rockwell",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Command_and_Service_Modules,_Apollo_-105,_ASTP_Mockup_-_DPLA_-_a0ec1c586f20e26eb3f3b857f4fd819b_(page_2).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 15.833,
          "end": 18.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 18.133,
          "end": 21.767,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 21.783,
      "end": 28.203,
      "text": "Paul C. Fisher spent around $1 million of his own private capital to develop the pen.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wellcome Collection",
        "title": "Sir John Fisher. Oil painting by John Prescott Knight, 1842.",
        "credit": "Wellcome Collection",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://wellcomecollection.org/works/kaw2xzdg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 21.767,
          "end": 24.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 24.133,
          "end": 28.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.203,
      "end": 35.823,
      "text": "Fisher patented the AG7 anti gravity pen in 1965 using pressurized nitrogen gas.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Propiska spOLe\u010dn\u011b.jpg",
        "credit": "V0lkanic",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Propiska_spOLe%C4%8Dn%C4%9B.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.2,
          "end": 35.833,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 35.823,
      "end": 43.773,
      "text": "NASA ordered 400 pens in 1968, and the Soviet Union later bought 100 for Soyuz missions.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Soyuz 19 (Apollo Soyuz Test Project) spacecraft.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soyuz_19_(Apollo_Soyuz_Test_Project)_spacecraft.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 35.833,
          "end": 39.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 39.8,
          "end": 43.767,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 43.773,
      "end": 51.151,
      "text": "Both space agencies ended up adopting the exact same pen because NASA never spent millions developing a space pen.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Art Institute of Chicago (CC0)",
        "title": "Marriage Consultation",
        "credit": "Edward Fisher\nIrish, 1730-1785",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://www.artic.edu/artworks/80167"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 43.767,
          "end": 51.5,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
